Q: Printing Unicode code point to console using int intead of \uNNNN A: <p>If you know ahead of time that the value is in the Basic Multilingual Plane (U+0000 to U+FFFF) you can just cast the number to <code>char</code> which represents a UTF-16 code point:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public static void PrintChar(int codePoint)
{
    Console.WriteLine((char) codePoint);
}
PrintChar(8364);
</code></pre>
<p>If you <em>don't</em> know that, use <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.char.convertfromutf32?view=net-10.0" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Char.ConvertFromUtf32(Int32)</code></a> which handles the whole of Unicode.</p>

Q: asynchronously download http webpages in tcl A: <p>Look into <a href="https://core.tcl-lang.org/tips/doc/trunk/tip/328.md" rel="nofollow noreferrer">TIP328</a> paragraph about <em>Asynchronous Communications</em>:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code> proc get url {
     http::geturl $url -command [info coroutine]
     yield
 }
 proc main {} {
     set t [get http://wiki.tcl.tk/4]
     puts [http::data $t]
     http::cleanup $t
 }
 coroutine m main
</code></pre>
